===
# Mathematical Equations with LaTeX

This presentation demonstrates the LaTeX block feature in SlideDeckML

===
## Simple Equation

The quadratic formula:

```latex
x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
```

===
## Einstein's Famous Equation

```latex
E = mc^2
```

This equation shows the relationship between energy and mass.

===
## Integrals and Limits

```latex
\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx = F(b) - F(a)
```

And a limit:

```latex
\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{1}{x} = 0
```

===
## Matrices

```latex
\begin{pmatrix}
a & b \\
c & d
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
x \\
y
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
ax + by \\
cx + dy
\end{pmatrix}
```

===
## Greek Letters and Summations

The sum of a series:

```latex
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n^2} = \frac{\pi^2}{6}
```

===
## Complex Equation

Schrödinger equation:

```latex
i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\Psi(\mathbf{r},t) = \left[-\frac{\hbar^2}{2m}\nabla^2 + V(\mathbf{r},t)\right]\Psi(\mathbf{r},t)
```

===
## Binomial Theorem

```latex
(x + y)^n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} \binom{n}{k} x^{n-k} y^k
```

===
## Maxwell's Equation

```latex
\nabla \times \mathbf{E} = -\frac{\partial \mathbf{B}}{\partial t}
```

One of Maxwell's fundamental equations of electromagnetism!

